[I] The extensible editor for structured binary data

[T] GNU Poke, not limited to editing basic entities such as bits and bytes,
[T] it provides a full-fledged procedural, interactive programming language
[T] designed to describe data structures and to operate on them.

[U] https://www.jemarch.net/poke

